{"availability":"available","full":"cran/difNLR","name":"difNLR","description":":exclamation: This is a read-only mirror of the CRAN R package repository.  difNLR — DIF and DDF Detection by Non-Linear Regression Models  Report bugs for this package: https://github.com/adelahladka/difNLR/issues","category":"Other","language":"R","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2016-11-09T18:27:59Z","updated":"2025-11-19T15:35:17Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://shiny.cs.cas.cz/ShinyItemAnalysis/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.665Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.665Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.665Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.665Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DIF and DDF Detection by Non-Linear Regression Models.","The difNLR package provides methods for detecting differential item functioning (DIF) using non-linear regression models. Both uniform and non-uniform DIF effects can be detected when considering a single focal group. Additionally, the method allows for testing differences in guessing or inattention parameters between the reference and focal group. DIF detection is performed using either a likelihood-ratio test, an F-test, or Wald's test of a submodel. The software offers a variety of algorithms for estimating item parameters.","Furthermore, the difNLR package includes methods for detecting differential distractor functioning (DDF) using multinomial log-linear regression model. It also introduces DIF detection approaches for ordinal data via adjacent category logit and cumulative logit regression models."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cran/difNLR/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"92de53b26c252b14bc92c99db84e91e7ade893d26ab22c5ae3dce9267b5a262e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"DIF and DDF Detection by Non-Linear Regression Models.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cran/difNLR/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"92de53b26c252b14bc92c99db84e91e7ade893d26ab22c5ae3dce9267b5a262e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cran/difNLR/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-11-19T15:35:17Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cran/difNLR/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:22:50.770Z","hash":"92de53b26c252b14bc92c99db84e91e7ade893d26ab22c5ae3dce9267b5a262e","originalBytes":3497,"storedBytes":3497,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["difnlr","dif","package","regression","version","detection","item","using","ddf","differential","functioning","github","hladka","journal","martinkova","models.","online","test","algorithms","approaches","cite","cran","detecting","development","devtools","educational","estimation","focal","get","group.","help","install","install.packages","logit","methods","new","newest","non-linear","please","reference","try","accounting","additionally","adelahladka","adjacent","allows","any","application","approach","available","behavioral","between","both","brabec","bug","case","category","codecov","considering","contact","coverage","cranlogs","cs.cas.cz","cumulative","current","data","description","detected","detection.","differences","directly","distractor","drabinova","easiest","effects","either","estimating","f-test","fairness","find","first","function","functionalities","functioning.","furthermore","generalized","getting","ghversion","guessing","guessing.","here","inattention","includes","installation","introduces","issue","iterative","just","leave","likelihood-ratio","log-linear","logistic","measurement","message","method","model.","models","multinomial","need","non-irt","non-uniform","nonlinear","offers","ordinal","parameters","parameters.","performed","provided","provides","publications","r-cmd-check",